      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To build a persuasive case, emphasize the introduction of modern infrastructure, such as railways and telegraph lines, which spurred internal connectivity and trade. You can also argue that colonial powers implemented formalized legal and administrative structures, providing a framework for modern governance and bureaucracy. Furthermore, the introduction of Western-style education and standardized systems of record-keeping offered foundational tools for future nation-building. Remember to frame these elements not as gifts, but as enduring legacies upon which post-colonial states had to build.",
      "source": "target",
